From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Gehrig Wilcox <lougehrig10@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 18:55:57 -0600
Subject: [PATCH 1/4] Mamba1 selective scan: deterministic backward mode

selective_scan_bwd accumulates dA, dB, dC, dD and ddelta_bias with
gpuAtomicAdd, so their float summation order (and bits) change run to run.

Add a deterministic mode: every (batch, channel) block stores its partial
result into its own float32 workspace slot, and the host reduces the
workspace with fixed-order kernels. dB/dC for input-dependent B/C are
processed in channel slices bounded by a memory budget; the running sum
continues across slices so the result is independent of the budget.

The mode is selected per call (`deterministic` argument of
selective_scan_cuda.bwd). The Python wrappers pass
mamba_ssm.utils.determinism.use_deterministic_mode(), i.e.
set_deterministic_mode() / MAMBA_DETERMINISTIC / torch's
use_deterministic_algorithms. Default (non-deterministic) behavior is
unchanged. Real and complex weights are supported.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
